{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:AppendixSurreals.SurrealSqueeze","@type":"LeanModule","name":"AppendixSurreals.SurrealSqueeze","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.surreal_squeeze_hypothesis_not_necessary","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.surreal_squeeze_hypothesis_not_necessary","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-surreals/surreal-squeeze.lean#L166-L172","doc":"**`surreal_squeeze`'s hypothesis is sufficient but not necessary**, so the\nsharp criterion is a genuine strengthening rather than a restatement. At\n`ε = δ = 1/2` the criterion `ε⁴ < δ²` holds while `ε < δ²` fails, so the\noriginal lemma misses a case the squeeze actually covers. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.surreal_squeeze_fails_at_eps_cubed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.surreal_squeeze_fails_at_eps_cubed","kind":"theorem","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-surreals/surreal-squeeze.lean#L151-L164","doc":"**The asserted mass gap `Δ_q ≍ ε³` does not clear the squeeze.**\n\nAt `δ = ε³` the cost is `ε⁵`, strictly *below* the budget `ε³` — the opposite of\nwhat the squeeze is invoked to show. So \"every non-trivial excitation has\n`δ ≥ Δ_q`\" does not follow from this inequality.\n\nScope-(a) (AGENTS.md §\"Before declaring refuted\"): this refutes the *inference*,\nnot the gap. `Δ_q ≍ ε³ > 0` is established in that block by a separate route and\nis untouched here, and nothing excludes a squeeze whose threshold is `ε³`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.surreal_squeeze_marginal_at_eps_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.surreal_squeeze_marginal_at_eps_sq","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-surreals/surreal-squeeze.lean#L145-L149","doc":"**The marginal case is real, and it sits at `δ = ε²`** — an exact equality,\nwhich is what `δ = 0` was mistakenly credited with. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.surreal_squeeze_fails_at_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.surreal_squeeze_fails_at_zero","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-surreals/surreal-squeeze.lean#L131-L142","doc":"**At `δ = 0` the squeeze FAILS; it does not degenerate to an equality.**\n\n`rem:yang-mills-surreal-bound` said it \"degenerates to the marginal equality at\n`δ = 0`\". The left side is `0` and the right side is `ε³ > 0`, so the inequality\nis false there, with no equality anywhere near it. The block's conclusion —\nthat the only zero-cost excitation is the trivial one — survives, but by this\nfailure rather than by a degeneracy. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.surreal_squeeze_threshold","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.surreal_squeeze_threshold","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-surreals/surreal-squeeze.lean#L118-L129","doc":"**The threshold is `ε²`.**  The squeeze holds precisely for `|δ| > ε²`.\n\nThis is the fact that matters downstream: the millennium-bound remarks read the\nsqueeze as certifying a gap, and the gap they assert is `ε³`, which is *below*\nthis threshold. See `surreal_squeeze_fails_at_eps_cubed`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.surreal_squeeze_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.surreal_squeeze_iff","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-surreals/surreal-squeeze.lean#L111-L116","doc":"**The squeeze, exactly.**  Clearing `ε⁻¹` reduces the inequality to a\ncomparison of `ε⁴` against `δ²` — no infinitesimality or domination hypothesis\nneeded, only `0 < ε` so the multiplication preserves the order. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.surreal_squeeze_needs_domination","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.surreal_squeeze_needs_domination","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-surreals/surreal-squeeze.lean#L91-L100","doc":"**The domination hypothesis is load-bearing.**  Drop `ε < δ²` and the lemma\nis false: at `ε = 9/10`, `δ = 1/10` we get `δ²·ε⁻¹ = 1/90 ≈ 0.011` while\n`ε³ = 729/1000 = 0.729`, so the cost does *not* exceed the budget.\n\nRecorded as a theorem rather than a comment so the falsifiability check of\nAGENTS.md §\"Strict Lean Discipline\" item 8 is machine-checked, not asserted.\nIt is also what distinguishes this from the tautology it replaces. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.surreal_squeeze_gap_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.surreal_squeeze_gap_pos","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-surreals/surreal-squeeze.lean#L84-L89","doc":"The same statement as the strict positivity of the gap, which is the form\nthe millennium-bound remarks consume (\"the cost strictly exceeds the budget\"). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.surreal_squeeze","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.surreal_squeeze","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/appendix-surreals/surreal-squeeze.lean#L67-L82","doc":"**Surreal squeeze.**  In any linearly ordered field, if `ε` is a positive\ninfinitesimal (`0 < ε < 1`) dominated by the standard-scale deviation\n(`ε < δ²`), then the cost `δ²·ε⁻¹` strictly exceeds the budget `ε³`.\n\nThis is `lem:surreal-squeeze` as stated in the `.md`, and it is the step every\nmillennium-bound remark in the appendix invokes. It holds over `ℝ(ε) ⊂ No`,\nwhich is where the `.md` places it — **not** over `ℝ`, where it is false.\n\nFalsifiability check (AGENTS.md §\"Strict Lean Discipline\" item 8): drop\n`hεδ` and take `δ² = ε/2`; then `δ²·ε⁻¹ = 1/2` while `ε³` can exceed `1/2`.\nThe hypothesis is doing work. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:lem:surreal-squeeze","label":"lem:surreal-squeeze","md":"quantum-observable-universe/appendix-surreals/surreal-squeeze.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}